      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "perltidy through 20160302, as used by perlcritic, check-all-the-things, and other software, relies on the current working directory for certain output files and does not have a symlink-attack protection mechanism, which allows local users to overwrite arbitrary files by creating a symlink, as demonstrated by creating a perltidy.ERR symlink that the victim cannot delete.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
